4:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - people: Joanna shared how rewarding it was to see her written work performed, drawing inspiration from real life and imagination to create characters.\n  - an idea: Joanna got ideas for characters from people she knows, things she saw, and her imagination, seeing them take shape with wants and worries.\n  - ideas: Joanna mentioned getting ideas from people she knows, things she saw, and her imagination, which take shape into characters.\n  - awesome characters: Joanna writes about \"wild worlds with awesome characters\" and is now in a writers group, feeling motivated by inspirational people.\n  - wild worlds: Joanna uses writing to create wild worlds with awesome characters and as an expression of feelings.\n  - picture: Nate complimented Joanna's drawings, asking what inspired them. Joanna previously mentioned seeing her writing acted out and Nate complimented a hiking picture.\n  - a person: Joanna experienced seeing characters and dialogue she wrote acted out, calling it an amazing and rewarding experience that was the third time this has happened.\n  - seeing all of the characters and dialogue I wrote being acted out: Joanna experienced seeing all of the characters and dialogue she wrote being acted out, which was rewarding and the third time this has happened to her.\n  - motivation: Joanna's cork board has inspiring quotes/pictures for motivation and creativity. She gains motivation from having someone to support her.\n  - characters: Joanna saw characters she wrote acted out on the big screen for the third time, finding the experience rewarding. Nate inquired about the character on the left in a shared photo.\n  - artist: Joanna, an artist, successfully set up meetings with movie producers, discussing her script and vision which includes elements of self-discovery. She feels hopeful and inspired.\n  - feelings: Writing is a way for Joanna to express her