h her writers group about a girl's journey to find her true home. She finds the work rewarding and emotional.\n  - seeing all of the characters and dialogue I wrote being acted out: Joanna experienced seeing all of the characters and dialogue she wrote being acted out, which was rewarding and the third time this has happened to her.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - journal: Joanna uses her journal as her rock while she is busy with writing projects, finding it helps her express feelings and heal.\n  - early writings: Joanna's early writings, found in old notebooks last week, include elements of self-discovery that movie producers found interesting.\n  - movie script: Joanna is filming a movie based on her road-trip script. She previously hoped for big-screen distribution, and Nate asked about future script submissions.\n  - writers group: Joanna shared her book with her writers group last week and received great feedback. She recently finished a cute little bookmark for one of the ladies at her writing club.\n  - sisterhood: Joanna watched a story exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams, which she recommended. She also finished writing her book last week after many late nights and edits.\n  - dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness: Joanna mentioned a page with dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness for her next movie; she finds the story deep and emotional.\n  - Jo: Joanna (Jo) asked Nate if he celebrated good feedback people are connecting with his writing. Previously, she asked about a couple he met while walking Max.\n  - passion: Joanna's writing is a huge part of her; Nate turned his passion for gaming into a career by winning an international tournament.\n  - writing gig: Joanna had an audition yesterday for a writing gig, feeling a mix of excitement and anxiety afterward. Nate previously encourage